# Mobile / tablet / landscape QA (MyDSP style)

Encode these preferences so future agents do **not** reintroduce clutter or overlapping chrome.

## Thumb CTA bars — deprecated (content-first)

- **Do not use** fixed bottom `.thumb-cta-bar` create clusters on phone / short landscape. See `mobile-content-first-chrome.mdc`.
- Create / Add / New actions live in **PageHeader** (always visible on phone) + `OverflowMenu`, quick-add, or empty states.
- Legacy `.thumb-cta-bar` CSS may remain for measured offsets / Job Detail nav until fully removed — new pages must not add thumb create bars.
- **Never** put page-level **Refresh** / **Sync now** in thumb bars (see `clean-sync-refresh-ux.mdc`). Non-interactive “Refreshing data” status is fine inline in the page.
- If a spacer still exists for Job Detail action bars, use **measured** `--thumb-cta-height` / `--job-detail-action-height` (ResizeObserver).

## No overlapping fixed chrome

- Fixed bars (thumb CTA, Job Detail action bar, bottom nav, floating banners/toasts) must **stack with measured offsets** — never guess two fixed heights that can wrap and collide.
- Floating banners/toasts clear `--thumb-cta-height` as well as the bottom nav.
- Job Detail: measure `--job-detail-action-height`; nav CTA sits above the action bar.

## Sticky stacks

- App header height → `--app-header-offset` (measured from `.app-header`, includes sync strip / meta).
- Markets sticky Tag/Yield filters sit **under** `--markets-toolbar-height`, not at the same `top` as the toolbar.
- Do **not** put `overflow: hidden` on `.app-header-row` / `.toolbar-cluster` — it clips More / Notifications menus.

## Markets chrome

- Prefer disclosure panels (**Assets / Timeframe / Format / Filters**) over permanent chip/select rows (see `disclosure-toolbar-panels.mdc`).
- Ownership · Alerts · Freshness · Types live under **Filters**, not stacked under search.
- Default timeframe **24H**; quiet poll ~**60s**; no noisy “Showing n/m prices” status.
- Search may stay visible; secondary filters must not.
- Section add buttons cover commodity / FX / index — creates live in PageHeader (content-first).

## Tablet (≥sm)

- PageHeader (or section empty states) must expose primary Add actions on phone **and** tablet — never rely on a bottom create bar.
- Portrait **and** landscape must both remain usable — equal priority with phone.

## Visual / UX style (carry forward)

- Minimal clear chrome; no overlapping buttons; full Edit pencils (no clipped icons).
- Cross-device sync for YouTube / News / Markets is imperative.
- Headers: Prices/section eyebrows+titles match My Crypto title scale.
